  "outcome": "partial",
  "summary": "Two rounds of the three-seat panel (opus, gpt-6-astra, gpt-6.1-sol) and a cross-model decision-trail review repaired the schema-derived landing build. Admission and execution now share one cached content slice for a node copy or a move into another root; a text range at a block edge is left to the drop's fitter, because its slice keeps open ancestors the fitter merges. A files drop checks one stand-in block per exposed DataTransfer file item. A keyboard step skips a landing redirect that leaves its parent, and an empty nodes list refuses source-missing. resolveDOMDropTarget returns no target while a move's pointer is over or alongside its own blocks, the handle's gutter included, before any container band. List reads a family's end from a lazy run index, so a hover check stays flat at any family size and a keyboard step is linear in siblings. The copied dnd.tsx lays out a nested gutter only for a node selection, or for a selection on a device without hover.",
