    "limits": "Drags are Playwright-emulated against a development build; no native OS drag, Safari, real touch device or production build ran, and the touch handle proof is Chromium emulation of hover: none. Earlier WebKit runs lost cases at ready() with the editor hidden before any action; two probes of 50 loads did not reproduce it, so its cause is unknown. The round-2 panel fixes had no third panel round; their proof is their own tests, a fuzz of the List index against the old walk and the probes in the decision log. Open, each with an owner in the plan: file-drop stand-in kind and hidden file counts, empty-anchor replacement on file drops, the one-entry check cache, collapse and unmounted landings, coverage lookups inside one container, Table anchor scans, the horizontal fallback, non-list blocks between list items, a family stepping past a family, source middleware idempotence, two selection subscriptions per handle, why a dragged gutter stays laid out, WebKit readiness, handle actions inside a containing selection, the summary-only details drop and a command insertion after an empty summary."
